<DocsLayout title="Architecture | Agent-Gantry">
  <h1>Architecture</h1>
  <p class="lead">Agent-Gantry separates discovery, retrieval, schema conversion, and execution so teams can adopt one layer at a time.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    <section class="card"><h3>Registry</h3><p>Stores tool definitions inferred from decorators, explicit schemas, modules, MCP servers, and framework adapters.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h3>Sync manager</h3><p>Fingerprints tool definitions and syncs changes to the vector store only when needed.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h3>Semantic router</h3><p>Embeds queries, searches candidate tools, applies score thresholds and optional rerankers, and can use LLM intent classification.</p></section>
    <section class="card"><h3>Execution engine</h3><p>Runs sync or async callables behind security policies, retries, rate limits, circuit breakers, telemetry, and callbacks.</p></section>
  </div>
  <h2>Runtime flow</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="text" code={`User prompt → semantic query → vector candidates → rerank / threshold → provider schema → model call → ToolCall → secure execution → telemetry/result`} />
  <h2>Choosing how tools are selected</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Semantic routing</strong> (the default) embeds the query and returns the top-k tools. It always returns k, whether or not any of them fit.</li>
    <li><strong>A reranker</strong> (<code>CohereReranker</code>, <code>CrossEncoderReranker</code>, <code>SystemOneReranker</code>) reorders that shortlist. It only reorders: its scores are never compared with a threshold, so it also returns tools for a query no tool can serve.</li>
    <li><strong>A selector</strong> (<code>SystemOneSelector</code>) replaces the search and asks a decision model about each entry, keeping those above <code>threshold</code>. It is the only one of the three that can return nothing, so choose it when declining matters. It sends the whole catalogue on every query, which suits tens to a few hundred entries.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Deployment modes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Library-only:</strong> import AgentGantry into an app and decorate existing tools.</li>
    <li><strong>Framework middleware:</strong> bridge into Microsoft Agent Framework, LangChain, LangGraph, LlamaIndex, CrewAI, and others.</li>
    <li><strong>Protocol service:</strong> expose tools through MCP or A2A for cross-agent interoperability.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
